{"name":"Sherry Cream","hex":"#f9e4db","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sherry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fortified wine produced in Jerez de la Frontera in Spain, or a similar wine produced elsewhere.","A variety of sherry."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sherry"},{"term":"cream","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The butterfat or milkfat part of milk which rises to the top; this part when separated from the remainder.","The liquid separated from milk, possibly with certain other milk products added, and with at least eighteen percent of it milkfat."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Cream-coloured; having a yellowish white colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cream"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sherry","blocks":[{"text":"Sherry is a fortified wine produced from white grapes grown around the city of Jerez de la Frontera in Andalusia, Spain. Sherry is a drink produced in a variety of styles made primarily from the Palomino grape, ranging from light versions similar to white table wines, such as Manzanilla and fino, to darker and heavier versions that have been allowed to oxidise as they age in barrel, such as Amontillado and oloroso. Sweet dessert wines are also made from Pedro Ximénez or Moscatel grapes, and are sometimes blended with Palomino-based sherries."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/DO_Jerez_location.svg/330px-DO_Jerez_location.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sherry"},{"title":"Cream","blocks":[{"text":"Cream is a dairy product composed of the higher-fat layer skimmed from the top of milk before homogenization. The butterfat, which is less dense, rises to the top and is skimmed off, resulting in gravity cream. The industrial production of cream instead uses centrifugal separators to make separator cream. Cream is often sold in grades defined by their butterfat content. It contains high levels of saturated fat, in ascending proportion from light cream to heavy cream."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/01_Mmm..._Apple_Crisp_with_Whipped_Cream.jpg/330px-01_Mmm..._Apple_Crisp_with_Whipped_Cream.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cream"},{"title":"Cream (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Cream is the color of the cream produced by cattle grazing on natural pasture with plants rich in yellow carotenoid pigments, some of which are incorporated into the fresh milk. This gives a yellow tone to otherwise-white milk at higher fat concentrations. Cream is the pastel colour of yellow, much as pink is to red. By mixing yellow and white, cream can be produced."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Milk_heavy_cream_B.jpg/330px-Milk_heavy_cream_B.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cream_(colour)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Del_Duque_Amontillado_Sherry.jpg/500px-Del_Duque_Amontillado_Sherry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Del_Duque_Amontillado_Sherry.jpg/1280px-Del_Duque_Amontillado_Sherry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Del_Duque_Amontillado_Sherry.jpg/500px-Del_Duque_Amontillado_Sherry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A glass of Amontillado sherry with olives","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADel_Duque_Amontillado_Sherry.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Sherry_de_la_Frontera_1775.jpg/500px-Sherry_de_la_Frontera_1775.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campa